## Run 4 — config hot-reload test

The config manager watches /etc/touchbar-engine/config.yaml and
/usr/share/touchbar-engine/config.yaml (system paths, per ADR-010
amendment). In dry-run, demo_config() is used for the INITIAL load,
but check_reload() runs every loop iteration and will pick up changes
to the watched system path. This is NOT hermetic to $HOME (by design,
the engine reads /etc/touchbar-engine/), but the daemon process itself
runs with hermetic HOME so it cannot read any user config.

### Ensure /etc/touchbar-engine/ exists, write a 1-page config
```
config installed: pages:
  - id: hotreload-test
    widgets:
```

### Start daemon (hermetic HOME), wait 2s, then touch the config file to trigger inotify
```
